  "brief": "`grid` is a table of whole numbers with `R` rows and `C` columns. Each query `{r1, c1, r2, c2}` asks for the sum of one rectangle of cells. It runs from row `r1` to row `r2` and from column `c1` to column `c2`. All four are included and count from 0. Write `rectangle_sums(grid, queries)`, which returns the sums as a `std::vector<long long>`, one per query, in order.",
