  "how": "Submit runs 10 hidden tests. Each answer must equal the expected value.",
  "solution": "#include <vector>\n\nstd::vector<long long> rectangle_sums(std::vector<std::vector<int>> grid, std::vector<std::vector<int>> queries) {\n    size_t rows = grid.size(), cols = grid[0].size();\n    std::vector<std::vector<long long>> p(rows + 1, std::vector<long long>(cols + 1, 0));\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < rows; ++i)\n        for (size_t j = 0; j < cols; ++j)\n            p[i + 1][j + 1] = p[i][j + 1] + p[i + 1][j] - p[i][j] + grid[i][j];\n    std::vector<long long> out;\n    for (const auto& q : queries)\n        out.push_back(p[q[2] + 1][q[3] + 1] - p[q[0]][q[3] + 1] - p[q[2] + 1][q[1]] + p[q[0]][q[1]]);\n    return out;\n}\n",
  "notes": [
    "`p[i][j]` holds the sum of the first `i` rows and first `j` columns. So row 0 and column 0 are zeros.",
    "Take the block up to row `r2` and column `c2`. Subtract the strip above and the strip to the left. Add back the corner removed twice.",
    "One pass over the grid and four lookups per query, so the work is $O(RC + q)$."
  ]
}
